    "result_text": "The full suite passes. There's only one test class (`AcceptanceTest`), and both its tests are green with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `locality` field, derived from an owner's city using the fixed city-to-region table.\n\nThe codebase already had a pattern for derived, read-only owner fields (`displayName`, `initials`, `membershipNumber`, `membershipTier`) computed in the MapStruct mapper and exposed on the generated `OwnerDto`. I followed that same idiom:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `locality` property to the `Owner` schema (so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field), documenting the city\u2192region mapping and the `UNKNOWN` fallback.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"locality\", expression = \"java(locality(owner))\")` to `toOwnerDto`, plus a fixed `CITY_REGION` table (`Sydney\u2192NSW, Melbourne\u2192VIC, Brisbane\u2192QLD`) and a `locality(owner)` helper that returns the canonical region or `\"UNKNOWN\"` when the city isn't in the table.\n\nThe derivation is a pure function of `city`, so no entity/persistence changes were needed \u2014 the region is computed on every read. Both acceptance tests (`coreDerivesRegionForKnownCity` \u2192 `NSW` for Sydney, and `functionalityUnknownCityIsUnknown` \u2192 `UNKNOWN`) pass, and the full test suite is green.",
